    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2018-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Rearranging the terms, notice that the expression in the question is equal to: \\[\\begin{align*}&1 + (3-2) + (5-4) + \\cdots +\\\\ &(2017-2016) + (2019-2018). \\end{align*}\\] Each term is equal to \\(1,\\) and there are \\(\\frac{2019-1}2+1 = 1010\\) terms, so the total sum is \\(1010\\cdot1 = 1010.\\)\n\nThus, E is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Pair each positive odd number after \\(1\\) with the even number just before it.",
        "Count how many \\(1\\)’s remain after pairing."
      ],
